-- lib/portal.hypercubical — Results Arrive by Transport (workflow/hyperactivity.cub
-- `results-arrive-by-transport`):
--   A researcher's workspace W holds types and constructions. When any result r : P B is
--   published anywhere in the content-addressed store alongside a demonstrated identity
--   e : A ≡ B (or a multi-hop chain of identities A ≡ B₁ ≡ ... ≡ Bₙ), cubical transport
--   delivers r directly into W as a native theorem of P A — with zero manual porting.
--
-- Proved here:
--   1. `portal-arrive`: single-hop transport arrival of a result r : P B across e : A ≡ B.
--   2. `portal-chain`: multi-hop identity composition across arbitrary chains of demonstrated
--      identities (`IdChain`), transporting results end-to-end.
--   3. `portal-roundtrip`: transporting across e then sym e recovers the original result
--      up to a cubical path (lossless bidirectional portal transport).
--   4. `portal-functorial`: composing two portal arrivals across e1 : A ≡ B and e2 : B ≡ C
--      agrees with arriving directly across concat e1 e2.
import "observation.hypercubical"



